<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles, Duke of Lower Lorraine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">953–c. 993</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Charles of Lorraine</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles (953–c. 993) was a Carolingian prince, younger son of the West Frankish king Louis IV and brother of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-i">Lothair</a>. Emperor Otto II made him Duke of Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a> in 977. After the death of his nephew Louis V in 987 he claimed the West Frankish crown against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugh-capet">Hugh Capet</a>, but he was betrayed and captured at Laon in 991 and died in captivity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-duke-of-lower-lorraine.jpg" alt="Charles, Duke of Lower Lorraine" width="320" height="153" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: fr.numista.com · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Denier_Struck_at_Laon_by_Charles_of_Lorraine_as_King_of_France,_987%E2%80%93990.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
